  "notes": [
    "-AR verb with a spelling change: **z→c before e** to preserve the /s/ (Latin America) or /θ/ (Spain) sound, since \"ze\" is not a standard Spanish spelling. This affects the yo form of the pretérito indefinido (abracé, not *abrazé) and every form of the subjuntivo presente and the usted/nosotros/ustedes imperative forms (abrace, abracemos, abracen).",
    "No stem change — this is purely an orthographic adjustment, not a stem-changing pattern.",
    "Past participle is regular: **abrazado**.",
    "*Ella abrazó a su hermana en el aeropuerto.* (\"She hugged her sister at the airport.\")",
    "*Espero que nos abracemos pronto.* (\"I hope we hug soon.\")",
    "Related: *el abrazo* (hug, noun), *abrazarse* (reflexive, \"to hug each other/one another\"), other -zar verbs share this same spelling pattern (rechazar, empezar, alcanzar, cruzar)."
  ],
